        </view>
        <style>
          <style-rule element='cell'>
            <format attr='height' value='124' />
          </style-rule>
        </style>
        <panes>
          <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-disallow'>
            <view>
              <breakdown value='auto' />
            </view>
            <mark class='Shape' />
            <encodings>
              <shape column='[federated.0ssh9xq09r963w1fpxhpm1lr0mvp].[none:Calculation_121456520101380096:nk]' />
            </encodings>
            <customized-tooltip show-buttons='false'>
              <formatted-text>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='11'>Below you have the definitions of each one of our metrics and views.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='11'>Data is available from Oct.2023 onwards.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#4e79a7' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='11'>Adoption</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>For adoption, we established a logic that consists of identifying who is the picker and </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>if they have two picker_ids active in that period.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>- If they do, they are considered using Both logins; </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>- If they used only the new one, we consider that he is using the New login; </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>- The last case is when they are using only the Old login.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#4e79a7' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='11'>Operational Metrics</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>In this part, you can see the results period over period regarding the picker&apos;s </run>
                <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Medium'>operational results</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>They are broken down as </run>
                <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Medium'>store</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>, </run>
                <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Medium'>picker</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>, and whether the vendor </run>
                <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Medium'>adopted the new flow or not</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>. </run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>Until 21.03.2024 only 5 stores from Viva Supermarket (UAE) chain have adopted the new flow.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#4e79a7' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='11'>Standard deviation of orders within a vendor</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>This is a specific metric regarding </run>
                <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Medium'>orders within the vendor</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>. The idea here is to identify </run>
                <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Medium'>who are the vendors that are concentrating many orders under the same picker account</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>. This is possibly a piece of evidence that pickers still are using the same account.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'>The mathematical logic is that </run>
                <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Medium'>high standard deviations</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'> are </run>
                <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Medium'>associated</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'> to an </run>
                <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Medium'>unbalanced</run>
                <run fontname='Tableau Medium'> relation between orders distributed to the pickers.</run>
              </formatted-text>
            </customized-tooltip>
            <style>
              <style-rule element='mark'>
                <format attr='mark-labels-cull' value='true' />
                <format attr='shape' value='Bug Tracking/light.png' />
                <format attr='mark-labels-show' value='false' />
              </style-rule>
              <style-rule element='pane'>
                <format attr='minheight' value='-1' />
                <format attr='maxheight' value='-1' />
              </style-rule>
            </style>
          </pane>
        </panes>
        <rows />
        <cols />
        <tooltip-style tooltip-mode='sticky' />
      </table>
      <simple-id uuid='{4AFA8142-A56B-43B9-B9AD-67AF89CBAD87}' />
    </worksheet>
